#
# Elecrow DIS08070H (CrowPanel ESP32 HMI 7.0") flash modules - the console, the external RAM
#
# The clock (dmclk) is the one of the mcu (configs/mcu/esp32s3/esp32s3fn16r8/flash.dmd).
#
# The console: UART0 on the pads of the ROM's console (GPIO43 TX, GPIO44 RX) that the USB-UART bridge of the board is wired to, 921600 8N1
# (board/elecrow-dis08070h/uart0.ini of dmuart); dmtty attaches a tty to it, so the shell runs there. /dev/ttyUSB0 on the host.
dmuart driver=board/elecrow-dis08070h/uart0.ini

#
# The external RAM: the 8 MB octal PSRAM of the module (WROOM-1-N4R8) behind the memory SPI (dmqspi), mapped into the address space and put
# at the end of the default heaps (it needs the clock of dmclk: driver_order). The chip and the bus are the same as on esp32s3-lcd28 (its
# ini of dmpsram is used: nothing in it is board specific).
dmqspi
dmpsram driver=board/esp32s3-lcd28.ini

#
# /ext is the last 1.9 MB of the 4 MB flash of the module (0x220000, board.cmake). dmflash exports it as the block node
# /dev/dmflashx/ext (the firmware does the erasing and programming from the internal RAM with the caches off: dmod-boot,
# src/arch/xtensa/lx7/flash.c), dmlittlefs keeps a littlefs on it, which the "ext" service (services/ext.ini) mounts at /ext.
# A new flash has no file system: create it once with `mklittlefs /dev/dmflashx/ext` (ALL DATA IN IT IS LOST), or with
# `cmake --build <dir> --target format-ext`.
dmflash driver=board/elecrow-dis08070h/flash.ini
dmlittlefs
mklittlefs
